// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6668 new: ROMULUS ClickFix delivery platform rules (MSI install, delivery URLs, DeElevate64 Run key, decimal DWORD IP download, Stardock sideload
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6668
// Pull request author: harperjohnsai
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential DeElevator64.DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: 917c1620-70d6-41e6-b2d7-4067f9b66b68
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Harper Johns
// Date: 2026-11-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects `DeElevate64.exe` loading `DeElevator64.dll` from outside the Stardock folders in
//   Program Files. In the ROMULUS ClickFix chain the signed Stardock executable and a patched
//   `DeElevator64.dll` (one added import, `I++u.dll`) are installed together from an MSI into the
//   user profile; the DLL pulls in the loader that decodes a shellcode from `Build.dat`.
// False positives:
//   - Portable or per-user installations of Stardock products
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/chatgpt-custom-gpts-clickfix-rat
//   - https://blackpointcyber.com/blog/romulus-cncmachinerms/
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/entries/3rd_party/stardock/deelevator64.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cd44704e28312f874bfcdfcae656722035f5fc0c/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_stardock_deelevator64.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\DeElevate64.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\DeElevator64.dll") and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Stardock\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Stardock\\")))
